# Forgex CRM — Cursor Rules
# Read this entire file before touching any code.
# Every suggestion must be consistent with these rules.

## Project
- Name: Forgex CRM
- Product: Centralized CRM, project management, blog/content system, and client portal for Forgex Systems (AI & Automation Agency)
- Framework: Next.js 15 (App Router)
- Language: TypeScript strict mode — never use `any`, use `unknown` and narrow properly
- Styling: Tailwind CSS v4 + CSS variables (no CSS modules, no inline styles for new code)
- Database: Supabase (PostgreSQL + RLS + Realtime)
- Auth: Supabase Auth via @supabase/ssr
- Deployment: Vercel
- Design language: Forgex brand (forge-black + electric-lime) — see Design System below

## Import Alias
- One alias only: @/* → ./src/*
- Example: import { throwIfError } from '@/server/leads/utils'
- No other aliases (~, #, etc.) exist or should be used

