## Key Libraries — Always Use These, Never Substitute
- Server data:      @tanstack/react-query (useQuery, useMutation) — never raw useEffect+fetch
- Forms:            react-hook-form + zod
- Global state:     zustand
- Icons:            lucide-react (outline only, never -filled variants)
- Animations:       framer-motion
- UI primitives:    components/ui/ (Modal, Button, etc.) and components/forgex/
- Class merging:    clsx + tailwind-merge via cn() helper
- Dates:            date-fns
- Rich text:        @tiptap/react (blog editor + internal docs editor)
- Charts:           recharts
- Realtime:         Supabase Realtime (notifications channel only)

## Supabase Clients — Never Mix These Up
- Browser (client components): createClient from @/lib/supabase/client
- Server (server components, API routes): createClient from @/lib/supabase/server
- Middleware: createClient from @/lib/supabase/middleware
- Service role (RLS bypass): createServiceClient from @/lib/supabase/service
  — only use service client for: client portal invite, notification fan-out, cron jobs, ticket creation
- Never import from @supabase/supabase-js directly in app/ or components/

## Supabase Type
- ServerSupabase = SupabaseClient<Database>
- Import: import type { ServerSupabase } from '@/server/shared/require-session'
- Always pass supabase as a parameter into server functions — never create it inside
- Exception: createServiceClient() is called inside functions that need RLS bypass

## Session and Auth Patterns
- getSession()     → { user, supabase, role } — does not require a role
- requireSession() → same but throws ForbiddenError if no role assigned
- requireRole(roles: Role[]) → throws ForbiddenError if user role not in list
- Portal session:  getPortalSession() → { client, project, supabase } (client-portal routes only)
- Role hierarchy:  admin > manager > member > client (client = portal only)

## Server Function Signatures
- Standard style: (supabase: ServerSupabase, userId: string, ...params)
- Always match the existing style in the file you are editing

## API Route Pattern
- Routes are thin — 10-20 lines max
- Pattern: getSession() → requireRole() → validate with zod → call server function → return ok()
- Always use response helpers from @/lib/api/responses (ok, created, badRequest, unauthorized, forbidden, notFound, conflict, serverError)
- Always use handleRouteError from @/server/shared/handle-route-error for catch blocks
- Validate all inputs with zod before use — client schemas in lib/validations/, API schemas in lib/validations/*-api.ts

## Error Handling
- throwIfError(error) — throws SupabaseError on PostgrestError
- Error classes in @/server/shared/errors: UnauthorizedError, ForbiddenError, NotFoundError, ValidationError, SupabaseError
- handleRouteError maps these to correct HTTP responses

## Notifications (In-App Only — No Email)
- All notifications are in-app only. No email notifications exist.
- Insert into notifications table via server/notifications/notifications.server.ts
- Use Supabase Realtime to push to the browser — subscribe in useNotifications hook
- Never call any email service for notification purposes
- Notification types: lead_assigned | follow_up_due | ticket_raised | blog_needs_review | task_assigned | project_updated | client_invited | comment_needs_moderation

