## Migrations Naming Convention
- Primary folder: supabase/migrations/
- Sub-folders by feature: supabase/migrations/{feature}/
  - 00_core/        → extensions, enums, shared types
  - 01_auth/        → profiles, client_accounts
  - 02_leads/       → leads, lead_notes, lead_attachments
  - 03_projects/    → projects, members, milestones, updates, files
  - 04_tasks/       → tasks, task_comments
  - 05_blog/        → blog_posts, categories, comments, community_users
  - 06_content/     → content_calendar, internal_docs
  - 07_notifications/ → notifications, triggers
  - 08_portal/      → client_tickets, ticket_messages, RLS for portal
  - 09_rls/         → consolidated RLS policies (one file per table group)
  - 10_indexes/     → all performance indexes
  - 11_triggers/    → all DB triggers (timestamps, completion_pct, realtime)
- Naming inside each folder: NNN_description.sql (e.g. 001_create_leads.sql)
- Never modify existing migration files — always add new ones
- Always run migrations in folder order, then file number order within folder

