## Routing
- Prefer paths from src/constants/routes.ts — never hardcode when a ROUTES key exists
- Dashboard routes gated by middleware: requires auth + role (admin|manager|member)
- Client portal routes: requires client_accounts.status = 'active' + valid project scope
- Public blog: on forgex.systems (separate repo) — CRM only manages data

## What Cursor Must Always Do
- Read relevant existing files before writing any new code
- Match the exact patterns of existing server functions in the same module
- Never create a new Supabase client inside a server function — accept it as a parameter
- Never use `any` — use `unknown` and narrow
- Prefer ROUTES from @/constants/routes — add keys when introducing new paths
- Never install new packages without asking
- Always use throwIfError() for Supabase query errors
- Always use handleRouteError in API route catch blocks
- Always validate API inputs with zod before use
- For notifications: always insert via server/notifications/ — never write to notifications table directly in feature code
- For realtime: subscribe only in hooks, never in server components
- Use design tokens (forge-black, electric-lime, ash, --radius-card) — no hardcoded hex values in components

## What Cursor Must Never Do
- Never send email notifications — in-app only via notifications table + Supabase Realtime
- Never use raw useEffect+fetch for server data — use React Query
- Never import Supabase directly in components — go through lib/supabase/
- Never put business logic in API route files — delegate to server/ modules
- Never create the service Supabase client unless RLS bypass is explicitly needed
- Never skip zod validation on API inputs
- Never invent a Dialog primitive — use Modal from @/components/ui/Modal
- Never allow client portal users to access team-only data (always scope by project + client_account_id)
- Never hardcode lead stages, roles, or blog categories — import from constants/
